message.content:
{
  "42": {
    "document_id": "42",
    "label": "1",
    "explanation": "Lott (with Collins) announces an agreement he reached that resulted in specific provisions being included in the Collins-Lieberman FEMA legislation, and Collins credits Lott's 'insight and input' as having 'improved and strengthened' the bill. Under clarification (2), claiming a 'key role' in specific legislative provisions presented as beneficial (a stronger, more accountable FEMA after Katrina) counts as credit-claiming. This goes beyond welcoming others' work because the release explicitly frames the provisions as the product of Lott's agreement and suggestions."
  },
  "714": {
    "document_id": "714",
    "label": "1",
    "explanation": "Although the op-ed's predominant purpose is to profile and congratulate the U.S. Marshals Service, it contains an explicit credit claim citing a specific delivered benefit: 'I helped secure more than $3 billion in the fiscal year 2006 Homeland Security appropriations bill for ICE's domestic enforcement efforts, as well as funding for 250 additional criminal investigators.' Clarification (5) expressly includes explicit credit claims embedded in speech or op-ed releases that cite a specific delivered benefit."
  },
  "794": {
    "document_id": "794",
    "label": "1",
    "explanation": "In this speech release, Bond states: 'The new federal highway bill, which Bond co-authored, is providing Missouri with much-needed resources, including $1 billion in new money - more than $4 billion in total funding.' This is nearly identical to the codebook's clarification (5) example of an explicit credit claim embedded in a speech citing a specific delivered benefit ('the highway bill I co-authored is bringing Missouri $1 billion'). Other parts are position-taking, but this passage is decisive."
  },
  "805": {
    "document_id": "805",
    "label": "1",
    "explanation": "Shelby announces that the Department of Homeland Security will release $3,510 to the Homewood Fire Department in Alabama through the Assistance to Firefighters Grants Program. Under clarification (1), announcements of federal grants flowing to the senator's state count as credit-claiming even without an explicit 'I secured it,' because issuing the announcement associates the senator with delivering the benefit."
  },
  "1257": {
    "document_id": "1257",
    "label": "1",
    "explanation": "The headline - 'PARMA RECEIVES FIREFIGHTING GRANT THROUGH SEN. DEWINE'S BILL' - and text explicitly tie the $105,550 grant to DeWine: he 'wrote and passed the FIRE Act,' 'helped secure approximately $650 million' for it, and passed an updated version. This is a textbook claim of personal responsibility for federal funds flowing to his state under clarification (1) and (2)."
  },
  "1325": {
    "document_id": "1325",
    "label": "0",
    "explanation": "Dole's floor statement criticizes Democrats' filibuster of judicial nominees and defends the 'constitutional option.' It is pure position-taking and criticism of the opposing party with no claim of personal responsibility for any delivered benefit, matching negative clarification (1) (position-taking/criticism) and the Kerry negative example."
  },
  "1749": {
    "document_id": "1749",
    "label": "1",
    "explanation": "Hutchison announces she 'signed on as an original cosponsor of the Veterans Housing Benefits Enhancement Act of 2007,' legislation presented as beneficial to injured service members. Clarification (2) explicitly includes claims of cosponsorship of specific legislation, even just introduced, when presented as delivering benefits."
  },
  "1897": {
    "document_id": "1897",
    "label": "0",
    "explanation": "Martinez's statement applauds Congressman Putnam's efforts but declares he cannot support the Pombo bill in its current form and would join a filibuster unless the buffer is extended. This is pure position-taking on pending legislation (negative clarification (1)) and applauding another's work (negative clarification (3)); he claims no personal responsibility for any outcome."
  },
  "1927": {
    "document_id": "1927",
    "label": "1",
    "explanation": "Snowe announces $8.1 million included in the FY2006 MilCon-VA appropriations bill for the Portsmouth Naval Shipyard and notes 'this funding was requested by Snowe and Sen. Susan Collins,' plus her letter requesting veterans funding. This is a classic announcement of federal funds secured for her state under clarification (1), akin to the Talent positive example."
  },
  "2335": {
    "document_id": "2335",
    "label": "0",
    "explanation": "The release invites Indiana children to submit essays honoring 'Outstanding Hoosier Dads.' Essay contests are expressly excluded by negative clarification (4) (ceremonial content: 'essay contests'). The passing mention that parts of his Responsible Fatherhood Act were signed into law is incidental context in a release whose predominant purpose is the contest, per negative clarification (6)."
  },
  "2869": {
    "document_id": "2869",
    "label": "0",
    "explanation": "Jeffords' statement explains why he voted for the Kerry and Levin amendments on Iraq and criticizes the Administration's lack of an exit strategy. It is an explanation of a vote and position-taking with no claim of personal responsibility for any result, squarely within negative clarification (1) and similar to the Carper negative example."
  },
  "3252": {
    "document_id": "3252",
    "label": "1",
    "explanation": "The release announces 'SENATE ADOPTS NELSON AMENDMENT,' noting 'his amendment... passed on a bipartisan vote of 72 to 26' and calling it 'a victory for Nebraska's ranchers.' Under clarification (2), claiming authorship of a specific amendment that passed a chamber, presented as beneficial to his state's constituents, is credit-claiming."
  },
  "4022": {
    "document_id": "4022",
    "label": "1",
    "explanation": "Kennedy's floor statement introduces his own bill: 'Today I am introducing legislation to extend Medicare to all Americans... I call this approach Medicare for All,' presented throughout as delivering major benefits. Clarification (2) covers claims of authorship of specific legislation 'whether just introduced... when the legislation is presented as beneficial.' I considered negative clarification (6) (floor statements whose predominant purpose is arguing policy), but the statement's legislative purpose is the introduction of his named bill, not merely incidental mentions of past roles, so it is credit-claiming."
  },
  "4122": {
    "document_id": "4122",
    "label": "1",
    "explanation": "This oversight release announces a Coleman-Levin hearing and claims concrete results from the Subcommittee's investigation: 'Due to the Subcommittee's oversight, collections from delinquent Defense contractors skyrocketed by 4,415%... levies on payments to deadbeat federal contractors have jumped 746%, raking in an additional $122 million in back taxes.' Clarification (4) includes oversight releases that claim concrete results such as funds recovered because of the senator's investigation."
  },
  "4184": {
    "document_id": "4184",
    "label": "1",
    "explanation": "The headline and text announce that Kyl 'co-sponsored' an amendment ('The Kyl amendment to the Senate Budget Resolution') providing $352 million for 2,000 new Border Patrol agents, presented as a beneficial national-security measure. Under clarification (2), claims of sponsorship/cosponsorship of a specific amendment presented as delivering benefits are credit-claiming."
  },
  "4207": {
    "document_id": "4207",
    "label": "0",
    "explanation": "The release's core action is Cornyn sending a letter 'requesting that [Secretary Chertoff] give due consideration' to the IBWC levee proposal - advocacy/urging with no outcome claimed as his achievement, which negative clarification (2) excludes. His past amendment merely required a report to Congress, and his appropriations letter is another request; no delivered benefit is claimed. This resembles the 'urging an agency to act' category rather than the Lott positive example where a federal action had actually followed his appeal."
  },
  "4295": {
    "document_id": "4295",
    "label": "1",
    "explanation": "Murkowski announces she 'introduced her second piece of legislation' to permanently adjust Alaska's FMAP Medicaid formula, presented as protecting ~$40 million annually for Alaska, and also notes she 'helped win a two-year change... that provided the state with an additional $34.11 million.' This combines authorship of beneficial legislation (clarification (2)) with a claim of a previously delivered federal benefit for her state."
  },
  "4508": {
    "document_id": "4508",
    "label": "1",
    "explanation": "This is the same text as the codebook's positive example: Lott announces FEMA trailers and mobile homes moving to Mississippi for Katrina victims and notes the move 'follows the Senator's Monday appeal to President Bush,' claiming a causal role in prompting the federal action (clarification (3))."
  },
  "4677": {
    "document_id": "4677",
    "label": "0",
    "explanation": "Hutchison's release describes her questions at a subcommittee hearing, assurances received on BRAC, and her support for the Army's 'Grow the Force' request. She says she is 'encouraged to see $18 million in the emergency supplemental for facilities at Fort Hood' but does not claim to have secured it. This is welcoming/applauding an outcome without claiming a causal role (negative clarification (3)) plus position-taking ('I have supported increasing the Army's end strength'), not credit-claiming."
  },
  "4774": {
    "document_id": "4774",
    "label": "1",
    "explanation": "While the release includes advocacy (letters urging conferees to retain the provision), it also claims a concrete legislative achievement: 'Last month, the Senate unanimously approved an amendment offered by Senators Bayh and Richard Durbin' to end the Patriot Penalty, described as providing 'crucial assistance' to Guard and Reserve families. Under clarification (2), claiming authorship of an amendment that passed a chamber and is presented as beneficial is credit-claiming."
  }
}

{
  "157": {
    "document_id": "157",
    "label": "0",
    "explanation": "This is essentially an empty notice containing only a title about a committee markup on venture capital and education bills. There is no substantive content, no claim of responsibility, and no announced benefit, so there is nothing that satisfies the definition of credit-claiming."
  },
  "189": {
    "document_id": "189",
    "label": "0",
    "explanation": "Leahy's statement is a Judiciary Committee hearing statement arguing for cameras in federal courtrooms and criticizing administration secrecy. Under negative clarification (6), hearing statements whose predominant purpose is arguing policy are not credit-claiming; his mention of cosponsoring the Sunshine in the Courtroom Act and Televising Supreme Court Proceedings Act is incidental advocacy within a policy argument, not a claim of a delivered benefit."
  },
  "744": {
    "document_id": "744",
    "label": "0",
    "explanation": "Allard sent a letter requesting that the Air Force clarify permissible religious expression at the Academy. Under negative clarification (2), this is advocacy/a request urging an agency to act, with no outcome claimed as the senator's achievement."
  },
  "873": {
    "document_id": "873",
    "label": "1",
    "explanation": "The release announces that Medicare penalties will be waived for hurricane-affected seniors and explicitly frames the outcome as a response to Sen. Landrieu's letter ('Administrator finally responds to Sen. Landrieu's letter'; 'the testimony responds to urgent calls... made by U.S. Senator Mary L. Landrieu'). Under clarification (3), framing an agency decision as a response to the senator's letter or appeal is credit-claiming, even though the result is shared with Rep. Jefferson."
  },
  "964": {
    "document_id": "964",
    "label": "0",
    "explanation": "Landrieu and Kerry are calling for local contracts in Katrina/Rita rebuilding and writing the SBA to speed up loss verification. Under negative clarification (2), this is advocacy/a request urging an agency to act, with no outcome claimed as an achievement."
  },
  "1043": {
    "document_id": "1043",
    "label": "1",
    "explanation": "DeWine announces a $78,046 federal grant to the Troy Township Fire Department and explicitly claims authorship and passage of the FIRE Act that created the grant program, plus his role securing $650 million in appropriations. This matches clarification (1) (announcement of a federal grant flowing to his state) and clarification (2) (authorship of beneficial legislation) - a textbook credit claim like the positive examples."
  },
  "1139": {
    "document_id": "1139",
    "label": "0",
    "explanation": "Coleman's statement extends condolences on the death of Rep. Charlie Norwood. Under negative clarification (4), this is ceremonial content (condolences), and his hope that Congress continues Norwood's legacy is a wish, not a claim of a delivered benefit."
  },
  "1610": {
    "document_id": "1610",
    "label": "0",
    "explanation": "Reid's remarks at the CHIP enrollment ceremony urge the President not to veto the bill and criticize his opposition. This is position-taking and advocacy (negative clarification 1); Reid credits others (Baucus, Rockefeller, Grassley, Hatch) and claims no personal responsibility for a delivered benefit - indeed the bill has not yet been signed and faces a threatened veto."
  },
  "1736": {
    "document_id": "1736",
    "label": "0",
    "explanation": "Domenici is requesting an expedited hearing and markup on the Livestock Assistance Act he cosponsored. The release's predominant purpose is urging committee action, which negative clarification (2) explicitly excludes ('urging that a... hearing be held'). No outcome - no passage, funding, or delivered relief - is claimed as his achievement; the cosponsorship mention serves the advocacy request rather than presenting a delivered benefit."
  },
  "2368": {
    "document_id": "2368",
    "label": "1",
    "explanation": "Craig announces that the VA will expand veterans' health services in Lewiston, Idaho - a concrete federal benefit flowing to his state (clarification 1). He also implicitly claims a causal role, thanking the VA Secretary for his 'willingness to hear my concerns and - more importantly - respond to the needs,' which frames the decision as responsive to his advocacy (clarification 3)."
  },
  "2382": {
    "document_id": "2382",
    "label": "1",
    "explanation": "Landrieu and Coleman announce their introduction of the CARES Act (S. 1588) to require insurers to cover reconstructive surgery for children with birth defects - a claim of authorship/sponsorship of specific legislation presented as beneficial (clarification 2, which covers bills 'just introduced'). The release additionally credits Landrieu with intervening at DHS to secure treatment for an Iraqi child, another explicit credit claim."
  },
  "2697": {
    "document_id": "2697",
    "label": "1",
    "explanation": "Inouye announces $225,000 in federal funding to control coqui frogs on the Big Island and explicitly states 'I then went looking and found another federal funding source,' a direct personal claim of securing the money after OMB denied the request. This is a clear credit claim under the definition and clarification (1)."
  },
  "2827": {
    "document_id": "2827",
    "label": "0",
    "explanation": "Lieberman's National Review op-ed argues for staying the course in Iraq and against retreat - pure foreign-policy position-taking with no claim of personal responsibility for any delivered government benefit (negative clarification 1)."
  },
  "2895": {
    "document_id": "2895",
    "label": "1",
    "explanation": "While much of the release explains McCaskill's vote for the 9/11 Commission bill, it specifically notes 'The bill also contains McCaskill's amendment to provide whistleblower protection and collective bargaining rights for airport screeners,' claiming authorship of a specific provision included in legislation passed by the chamber and presented as beneficial. This satisfies clarification (2), distinguishing it from a mere vote explanation."
  },
  "3038": {
    "document_id": "3038",
    "label": "0",
    "explanation": "Snowe's statement supports Vice Admiral Allen's nomination as Coast Guard Commandant, praising his record and the outgoing Commandant. This is pure position-taking on a nomination at a committee hearing (negative clarification 1); she claims no personal responsibility for any delivered benefit, designation, or agency action."
  },
  "3143": {
    "document_id": "3143",
    "label": "1",
    "explanation": "Although framed partly as support for the farm bill, the release contains specific credit claims: 'Graham worked to include additional grant programs that could benefit research and training being conducted in South Carolina' and 'a Graham backed provision that would provide economic adjustment assistance... to textile manufacturers.' These are claims of securing specific beneficial provisions in a bill passed by the Senate (clarification 2), reinforced by the state agriculture commissioner thanking Graham for 'his efforts in securing passage.'"
  },
  "3149": {
    "document_id": "3149",
    "label": "1",
    "explanation": "Beyond noting Reed's support for the budget resolution, the release lists 'A provision championed by Reed to help establish an affordable housing fund' among the budget's contents, claiming a key role in a specific beneficial provision included in legislation that passed the Senate. This satisfies clarification (2) for claims of a 'key role' in specific provisions, distinguishing it from a simple vote explanation."
  },
  "3817": {
    "document_id": "3817",
    "label": "0",
    "explanation": "Sessions applauds the TVA Board's decision to proceed with the Bellefonte nuclear application. Under negative clarification (3), welcoming/applauding a decision made by others without claiming a causal role is not credit-claiming. His statement that Bellefonte 'has been a priority of mine' expresses longstanding support, not a claim that he prompted the Board's action."
  },
  "4328": {
    "document_id": "4328",
    "label": "1",
    "explanation": "Alexander and Corker announce a DOT decision providing Essential Air Service nonstop flights between Jackson, TN and Cincinnati - a federal benefit flowing to their state (clarification 1). The release also notes the senators 'wrote a letter in support of Jackson's application,' framing the favorable decision as responsive to their appeal (clarification 3)."
  },
  "4403": {
    "document_id": "4403",
    "label": "1",
    "explanation": "Domenici announces he is an original cosponsor of the R-HoPE Act and highlights provisions he 'first authored' and 'championed' to improve Medicare payments for rural providers, presented as delivering significant benefits to New Mexico's rural hospitals (up to a 15 percent revenue increase). Under clarification (2), claiming authorship/cosponsorship of specific beneficial legislation - even just introduced - is credit-claiming."
  }
}

{
  "50": {
    "document_id": "50",
    "label": "0",
    "explanation": "Reid's statement is purely a criticism of the Bush administration's 'head in the sand' position on global warming and expresses hope that a new announcement is genuine. Under negative clarification (1), this is pure position-taking and criticism of the administration with no claim of personal responsibility for any delivered outcome."
  },
  "57": {
    "document_id": "57",
    "label": "1",
    "explanation": "Kennedy 'introduced legislation' (the Human Cloning Ban and Stem Cell Research Protection Act) and the release repeatedly presents the bill as beneficial (unlocking cures, saving lives, banning cloning). Under clarification (2), claims of authorship/sponsorship of specific legislation count as credit-claiming 'whether just introduced... when the legislation is presented as beneficial.' The release also touts benefits for Massachusetts institutions, reinforcing the claim that Kennedy is delivering something good."
  },
  "89": {
    "document_id": "89",
    "label": "1",
    "explanation": "This is the codebook's positive example. Dorgan announces Bismarck State College's federal designation as a national center and states he 'authored legislation, which was signed into law, that created the National Center designation' - an explicit claim of personal responsibility for a delivered federal benefit (clarification items 1 and 2)."
  },
  "240": {
    "document_id": "240",
    "label": "0",
    "explanation": "Ensign's statement merely reacts to the Senate's confirmation of Michael Chertoff, praising his experience and saying he looks forward to working with him. Under negative clarification (1) and (3), this is a reaction/position statement about an action taken by others, with no claim of personal responsibility for any benefit."
  },
  "453": {
    "document_id": "453",
    "label": "0",
    "explanation": "Nelson explains why he voted against two Iraq withdrawal resolutions, advocating measurable goals rather than arbitrary dates. Under negative clarification (1), this is a vote explanation/position statement; he claims no personal responsibility for any delivered government action or benefit."
  },
  "597": {
    "document_id": "597",
    "label": "0",
    "explanation": "The release describes Lugar presenting the 'Dick Lugar Health and Fitness Award' to community recipients at his annual charity run/walk. Under negative clarification (4), this is ceremonial content - awards presented to others - with no claim of delivering a government action or benefit."
  },
  "656": {
    "document_id": "656",
    "label": "0",
    "explanation": "This is the codebook's negative example. Kerry's statement on the Dubai Ports deal is entirely criticism of the Bush administration's incompetence on port security; he claims no personal action or accomplishment (negative clarification 1)."
  },
  "918": {
    "document_id": "918",
    "label": "0",
    "explanation": "This is the codebook's negative example. Allard's release merely announces the time and place of a Greeley town meeting - constituent outreach logistics with no policy position and no claim of delivering any benefit (negative clarification 4)."
  },
  "967": {
    "document_id": "967",
    "label": "1",
    "explanation": "Shelby announces that HHS will release $3,305,732 to Talladega-area childcare/Head Start programs, noting his seat on the Appropriations Committee. Under clarification (1), announcements of federal funds flowing to the senator's state count as credit-claiming because issuing the announcement associates the senator with delivering the benefit."
  },
  "1021": {
    "document_id": "1021",
    "label": "1",
    "explanation": "Wyden and Smith announce that the Senate Appropriations Committee has approved funding they sought: $13 million for Oregon salmon recovery, $2 million for OSU ocean observation, and numerous other Oregon-benefiting programs. Under clarification (1), announcing federal funds flowing to the senator's state is credit-claiming, and Wyden's statement that 'the Federal dollars in this bill will support important programs' frames the funding as a delivered benefit."
  },
  "1957": {
    "document_id": "1957",
    "label": "1",
    "explanation": "Dodd and Lieberman announce that Bradley International Airport will receive a $2,250,000 federal grant for runway improvements, touting jobs and safety benefits for Connecticut. Under clarification (1), announcements of federal grants flowing to the senator's state count as credit-claiming even without an explicit 'I secured it.'"
  },
  "2318": {
    "document_id": "2318",
    "label": "1",
    "explanation": "Although much of the release is a letter urging Illinois state officials to act (which alone would be advocacy under negative clarification 2), Durbin embeds explicit credit claims: 'I helped secure an expedited environmental review from the federal government and facilitated the return of the project to the national priority list for federal funding.' Under clarification (3) and (5), claiming to have prompted/expedited agency actions and delivered federal benefits counts as credit-claiming even when embedded in an advocacy release."
  },
  "2807": {
    "document_id": "2807",
    "label": "0",
    "explanation": "Lincoln's release recognizes Arkansas Women in Agriculture month, applauding the proclamation signed by the Governor. Under negative clarification (4), this is ceremonial/commemorative content. The passing mention that she 'played a key role in the 2002 farm bill debate' is incidental background about her committee role, not a claim of a specific delivered benefit, and does not convert this ceremonial release into credit-claiming (negative clarification 6)."
  },
  "3482": {
    "document_id": "3482",
    "label": "1",
    "explanation": "Mikulski and Cardin announce a $294,980 federal SAFER grant to Allegany County firefighters, noting Mikulski's role on the subcommittee that funds the program and her fight to increase its funding. Under clarification (1), announcing federal grants flowing to the senator's state is credit-claiming because the announcement associates the senators with delivering the benefit."
  },
  "3577": {
    "document_id": "3577",
    "label": "0",
    "explanation": "Sarbanes's committee statement on the National Flood Insurance Program is predominantly a policy argument criticizing FEMA's preparedness and listing issues to review. His mention of having 'called on the President' is advocacy with no claimed outcome (negative clarification 2), and the reference to reforms he 'worked with Senator Bunning' on is incidental context within a hearing statement whose predominant purpose is arguing policy (negative clarification 6)."
  },
  "3659": {
    "document_id": "3659",
    "label": "0",
    "explanation": "Clinton 'welcomed' the NIOSH advisory board's recommendation to compensate Linde workers and urges Secretary Leavitt to adopt it; she also pledges to keep pressing for Bethlehem Steel workers. Under negative clarification (3), welcoming or applauding decisions made by others without claiming a causal role is not credit-claiming, and her continued pressing is advocacy with no outcome claimed (negative clarification 2)."
  },
  "3687": {
    "document_id": "3687",
    "label": "1",
    "explanation": "Bingaman announces that New Mexico State University has been awarded $599,691 in USDA funds for food safety research. Under clarification (1), announcing federal funds flowing to an institution in the senator's state counts as credit-claiming because the announcement associates the senator with delivering the benefit, even without an explicit 'I secured it.'"
  },
  "4208": {
    "document_id": "4208",
    "label": "1",
    "explanation": "Dorgan and Lott announce they are introducing the 'Media Ownership Act of 2007,' presenting it as beneficial legislation that protects localism and diversity against media consolidation. Under clarification (2), claims of authorship/sponsorship of specific legislation - 'whether just introduced' - count as credit-claiming when the legislation is presented as delivering benefits."
  },
  "4585": {
    "document_id": "4585",
    "label": "1",
    "explanation": "Schumer announces over $134,000 in federal fire grants to two Westchester County fire departments (part of nearly $3 million statewide) and notes he 'has pushed for additional funding' for the program. Under clarification (1), announcements of federal grants flowing to the senator's state constitute credit-claiming."
  },
  "4771": {
    "document_id": "4771",
    "label": "1",
    "explanation": "Although framed around a meeting, the release prominently claims that Clinton 'played a key role along with SMAC in preventing the removal of four C-130 Aircraft' and ties her to the BRAC Commission's decision to keep the aircraft at Stratton - a concrete, desirable outcome for her constituents. Under clarification (3), claiming a key role in prompting/influencing a government basing decision is credit-claiming; this goes beyond merely advocating for the base (negative clarification 2) because a past outcome is claimed as her achievement."
  }
}
